# Loading and empty states

Import from `@webonone/ui-kit`: **`LoadingState`**, **`ItemListEmpty`**.

## Unified platform loading overlay (required)

**WebOnOne core, Data, Email, and new platform-shell satellites** must show **one content-area overlay** for session, lazy-route, and page/data loads — header and sidebar stay visible; never stacked spinners.

```text
AppLayout
  PlatformLoadingProvider
  AppShell (onNavItemNavigate + optional onNavItemPrefetch)
  → <div className="relative min-h-full">
      <Outlet />
      <LoadingState overlay overlayScope="content" label={…} />
SessionRoleGate / session hooks → usePlatformLoading('Loading session…')
LazyRoute Suspense fallback → useDelayedRouteLoading('Loading page…'); return null
Pages / list fetches → usePlatformLoading(loading ? 'Loading …' : null)
```

| Hook / surface | Role |
|----------------|------|
| `PlatformLoadingProvider` | Wrap `AppLayout` content tree; owns the ref-counted loader registry |
| `usePlatformLoading(label)` | Session gate, page data fetch, editor load (`page` kind) |
| `useRouteLoading(label)` / `useDelayedRouteLoading(label)` | Lazy route chunk (`LazyRoute` only) — ~175ms delay (`route` kind) |
| `usePlatformOverlayLabel()` | **Read the single resolved overlay label in `AppLayout`** — do not compute it manually |
| `AppLayout` overlay | Sole visible loading UI; **`overlayScope="content"`** |

Hooks use **`useLayoutEffect`** to set/clear labels (avoids one-frame overlay gaps).

### Ref-counted registry + hide-linger (required)

`PlatformLoadingContext` keeps **`Map<id, label>`** loaders (one per `useId()`), split by `page` and `route` kind — **never a single label slot** (concurrent loaders would stomp each other and flicker). The overlay label resolves as: newest `page` loader if any, else newest `route` loader, else `null`. When the last loader clears, the overlay lingers **`HIDE_LINGER_MS` (200ms)** before hiding, so a quick clear→set hand-off (route chunk → page fetch) shows **one continuous overlay** instead of an off/on blink. Reference: `webonone-v2/frontend/src/features/shell/context/PlatformLoadingContext.tsx` (copy per service).

**Route every loading state through the registry** — including session loading. `AppLayout` calls `usePlatformLoading(sessionLoading ? 'Loading session…' : null)` and reads the final label from `usePlatformOverlayLabel()`; do not `??`-chain page/route/session labels by hand.

**Client-side local nav** — pass `onNavItemNavigate={createNavItemNavigate(...)}` on `AppShell` (from `@webonone/platform-nav`). Do not use per-service `withClientSideNavigation` on nav items. Optional `onNavItemPrefetch` from `<service>/app/routePrefetch.ts` for hover prefetch.

**Label source (all apps):** `const overlayLabel = usePlatformOverlayLabel()`. Feed the registry per app:

| App | Session feed into registry |
|-----|----------------------------|
| Data / Email satellite | `usePlatformLoading(sessionLoading ? 'Loading session…' : null)` in `AppLayout` — `sessionLoading = Boolean(accessToken) && !roleReady`; **exclude** `isBootstrapping` |
| WebOnOne core | Session via `SessionRoleGate` → `usePlatformLoading('Loading session…')` |

Do **not** manually compose `sessionLoading ? … : pageLabel ?? routeLabel` in `AppLayout` — the registry already resolves priority and applies hide-linger.

Context module (same API — copy per service):

| Service | Path |
|---------|------|
| WebOnOne v2 | `webonone-v2/frontend/src/features/shell/context/PlatformLoadingContext.tsx` |
| Data / Email | `<service>/frontend/src/features/auth/context/PlatformLoadingContext.tsx` |

Reference: `data/frontend/src/app/AppLayout.tsx`, `data/frontend/src/app/LazyRoute.tsx`, `webonone-v2/frontend/src/app/AppLayout.tsx`, `webonone-v2/frontend/src/features/session/components/SessionRoleGate.tsx`.

**Forbidden:** inline `"Loading…"` text in pages; per-page `<LoadingState overlay />`; `LazyRoute` fallback that renders visible `Spinner`/`LoadingState`; second overlay during `code` bootstrap in satellite `AppLayout`; `overlayScope="viewport"` in `AppLayout` (use viewport only for login/logout full pages).

**Exception:** platform inbound **`code` bootstrap** may use a page-content spinner during exchange only — not an AppLayout overlay. See [platform-shell-navigation.mdc](platform-shell-navigation.mdc).

**Cross-service nav:** full `window.location` navigation is expected per origin hop; destination must keep `AppShell` stable with content-scoped loading only.

**Embedded overlay (iframe peers):** when a peer runs inside the WebOnOne shell iframe, the **shell** owns the overlay during initial load; the embedded `PlatformEmbedLayout` must **defer its own overlay until it has emitted its first `content-ready`** (otherwise the shell overlay and the embed overlay stack = two overlays). Detail and the `content-ready` handshake live in [platform-shell-navigation.mdc](platform-shell-navigation.mdc).

## LoadingState (AppLayout + buttons)

Centered themed spinner + label.

| Prop | Notes |
|------|-------|
| `label` | Contextual: `"Loading tags…"`, `"Loading session…"`, `"Loading page…"` |
| `overlay` | **`true`** in **`AppLayout` only** — nowhere else |
| `overlayScope` | **`content`** (default) in AppLayout; **`viewport`** for login/logout standalone pages |

**Buttons:** **`Spinner size="sm"`** inside the button — not `LoadingState`.

Page hook example: `data/frontend/src/features/tags/pages/TagsPage.tsx`.

## ItemListEmpty

Centered empty-list message when **`items.length === 0`** inside or instead of `ItemList`.

Pass copy as children, e.g. `<ItemListEmpty>No tags found.</ItemListEmpty>`.

Reference: `data/frontend/src/features/tags/components/TagsList.tsx`.

